#!/bin/sh
# Runs the ffmpeg on PATH, except that its loudness meter reads every true
# peak at +5 dBTP, however far the sound is limited: a peak the limiter
# does not reach.
case "$*" in
  *ebur128=*) ;;
  *) exec ffmpeg "$@" ;;
esac
said=$(ffmpeg "$@" 2>&1)
code=$?
printf '%s\n' "$said" | sed 's/^\( *Peak: *\)[-+0-9.a-z]*/\15.0/' >&2
exit $code
